# The Baron's watch answers a crime somebody saw in Vallaki (F8 and F2's town watch; docs/rules/stealth.md,
# docs/voice/vallaki_guard.md). story/crime.gd counts the offence in crime_vallaki and stages a Town Guard beside the
# party, then plays theft, trespass or spell (a spell cast at someone; world/exploration/location_npcs.gd). Every way
# out clears the count: a fine, a word that works, or a fight.

~ theft
Town Guard [angry]: You there. Stop. Hands where I can see them. Stealing, in Vallaki, in festival week. The Baron will want that in the speech.
-> charge

~ trespass
Town Guard [angry]: That's a private house, and you were told to get out of it. In Vallaki that's a fine. The Baron is very fond of fines.
-> charge

~ spell
Town Guard [angry]: Hexing people in the street, are we? In Vallaki, in festival week? Witchcraft is a fine at best and a bonfire at worst, and the Baron is short of wicker.
-> charge

~ charge
if flag.crime_vallaki >= 2
Town Guard: Again? Fifty gold for the Baron's coffers, or the stocks. The stocks are full this week, mostly of people who frowned.
else
Town Guard: Twenty-five gold for the Baron's coffers, and we'll call it festival spirit.
endif
* [if flag.crime_vallaki < 2 and gold >= 25] Pay the twenty-five gold. -> pay_small
* [if flag.crime_vallaki >= 2 and gold >= 50] Pay the fifty gold. -> pay_large
* [if flag.crime_vallaki < 2 and gold < 25] We haven't got twenty-five gold. -> empty_purse
* [if flag.crime_vallaki >= 2 and gold < 50] We haven't got fifty gold. -> empty_purse
* [Persuasion DC 15] A misunderstanding. We were putting it back. -> let_off | not_buying
* [Deception DC 15] The owner sent us to fetch it. Go and ask. -> let_off | not_buying
* Refuse. -> refuse

~ not_buying
Town Guard: No. I've heard that one before, and so has the Baron, and he made it a crime to say it.
* [if flag.crime_vallaki < 2 and gold >= 25] Pay the twenty-five gold. -> pay_small
* [if flag.crime_vallaki >= 2 and gold >= 50] Pay the fifty gold. -> pay_large
* [if flag.crime_vallaki < 2 and gold < 25] We haven't got twenty-five gold. -> empty_purse
* [if flag.crime_vallaki >= 2 and gold < 50] We haven't got fifty gold. -> empty_purse
* Refuse. -> refuse

~ pay_small
gold -25
set crime_vallaki = 0
Town Guard [smile]: Lovely. The Baron thanks you for your contribution to the festival. All will be well.
-> END

~ pay_large
gold -50
set crime_vallaki = 0
Town Guard: Paid in full. Do it a third time and I'll have to remember your faces, and I'd honestly rather not.
-> END

~ empty_purse
gold -50
set crime_vallaki = 0
Town Guard: Then whatever you've got will do. Turn out your pockets. All of it. There. Now go and be poor somewhere quietly.
-> END

~ let_off
set crime_vallaki = 0
Town Guard: Fine. Fine! I didn't see anything. I never see anything. It's the only way to stay sane in this town.
-> END

~ refuse
Town Guard [angry]: Then it's the stocks, the hard way. Watch! To me!
combat watch_arrest
